[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 764,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 701,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 121506,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 267,
        "headingId": 701,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Fibroblastic reticular cell tumour (FRCT) is a neoplasm of putative stromal fibroblastic reticular cell origin.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-02-28T16:55:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 765,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 702,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 121507,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 267,
        "headingId": 702,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>9759/3 Fibroblastic reticular cell tumour</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-02-28T16:55:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 766,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 703,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 121508,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 267,
        "headingId": 703,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>2B31.7 Fibroblastic reticular cell tumour</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-02-28T16:55:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 767,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 704,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 121509,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 267,
        "headingId": 704,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> fibroblastic dendritic cell tumour; fibroblastic reticular cell sarcoma.</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> cytokeratin-positive interstitial reticulum cell tumour.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-02-28T16:55:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 768,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 705,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 121510,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 267,
        "headingId": 705,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-02-28T16:55:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 769,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 706,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 121511,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 267,
        "headingId": 706,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Isolated nodal disease is most common, but various extranodal sites can also be involved, such as the spleen, soft tissues, liver, lung, kidney, breast, adrenal gland, and bone {23755890; 25405526; 10632494; 24220998; 26893647; 26826404; 26893647}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-02-28T16:55:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 770,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 707,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 121512,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 267,
        "headingId": 707,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>The most common presentation is lymphadenopathy or a newly developed mass. Rarely, FRCT is an incidental finding or occurs concurrently with another malignancy {21284739; 32979929}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-02-28T16:55:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 771,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 708,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 121513,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 267,
        "headingId": 708,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>FRCT is rare, often presenting in the seventh decade of life (age range: 13&ndash;80&nbsp;years, median: 61&nbsp;years) {23755890; 26893647}. There is no sex predilection.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-02-28T16:55:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 772,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 709,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 121514,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 267,
        "headingId": 709,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-02-28T16:55:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 773,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 710,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 121515,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 267,
        "headingId": 710,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-02-28T16:55:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 780,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 717,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 121516,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 267,
        "headingId": 717,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>FRCT often forms a well-circumscribed tumour nodule. Tumour size is variable, ranging from 9&nbsp;to 160&nbsp;mm. Haemorrhage and necrosis can be present.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-02-28T16:55:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 774,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 711,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 121517,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 267,
        "headingId": 711,
        "headingText": "<p>FRCTs are characterized by spindle to oval cells, often arranged in a whorled, fascicular, sheeting, or storiform pattern and accompanied by a lymphoplasmacytic infiltrate. The degree of nuclear pleomorphism is variable, and multinucleated or giant tumour cells may be admixed. Thus FRCT shows overlapping morphological features with follicular dendritic cell sarcoma and interdigitating dendritic cell sarcoma. A characteristic, but neither invariable nor pathognomonic, feature is the presence of intercellular collagen fibrils.</p>\r\n<p>Ultrastructurally, the tumour cells show delicate cytoplasmic extensions and features reminiscent of myofibroblasts (elongated nuclei, filaments with occasional fusiform densities, moderate amounts of rough endoplasmic reticulum, well-developed desmosomal attachments in contiguous arrangements, and basal lamina&ndash;like material forming linear extracellular condensations) {9737236}.</p>\r\n\r\n<h5>Immunohistochemistry</h5>\r\n\r\n<p>The immunophenotype overlaps with that of myofibroblasts, with variable positivity for actin, desmin, and vimentin {7520705}. Two&nbsp;thirds of cases are cytokeratin-positive, with delicate cell processes being highlighted by the immunostain. L-caldesmon, fascin, vimentin, and EMA are often positive. The tumour should lack markers of follicular dendritic cell sarcoma (such as CD21 and CD35) and interdigitating dendritic cell sarcoma (S100), although there are rare reported cases with hybrid features of FRCT and follicular dendritic cell sarcoma {11598178; 25768257}. In cytokeratin-positive FRCT cases, metastatic carcinoma should be considered in the differential diagnosis.</p>\r\n&nbsp;",
        "timestamp": "2024-02-28T16:55:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 775,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 712,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 121518,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 267,
        "headingId": 712,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Diagnosis requires histopathological examination.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-02-28T16:55:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 776,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
